    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement \u2014 **all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`, with HTTP status codes unchanged** \u2014 is fully satisfied by the codebase, and I verified it holds across every rejection path.\n\n### What the code does\nAll 400/409/429 rejections on `POST /api/owners` are surfaced as exceptions and centralized in one place, `rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice`, where a single `detailBuild(...)` helper constructs a Spring `ProblemDetail`:\n\n- **`type`** \u2192 request URL, **`title`** \u2192 exception class name, **`status`** \u2192 from the HTTP status, **`detail`** \u2192 a human-readable message.\n- Returning `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` makes Spring serialize with `Content-Type: application/problem+json`.\n\nThe rejection sources it covers:\n- **400** \u2014 bean validation (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`), `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, `InvalidTelephoneException`, `InvalidEmailException`, `DisposableEmailDomainException`, `InvalidPostcodeException`, `FutureRegistrationDateException`\n- **409** \u2014 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`, `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException`\n- **429** \u2014 `OwnerDailyRegistrationLimitExceededException`\n\nThe construction lives in the one helper rather than being duplicated per handler, so the RFC7807 shape stays consistent and in a single responsibility.\n\n### Verification\n- The provided new test `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` (a 400 path) passes: exact content type `application/problem+json` and `$.status == 400`.\n- I additionally ran a temporary test exercising a **409** (duplicate identity), a **custom 400** (invalid telephone), and a **429** (daily limit); all three returned `application/problem+json` with all four required members present and the correct `status`. I then removed that temporary test.\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nNo source changes were needed \u2014 the specification is already met and verified end-to-end, so I made no edits rather than introduce unnecessary churn.",
